  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing disaster risk through sustainable land use and land ownership management in Liberia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to reduce the risk of the target communities to conflicts over land through peace-building and conflict resolution activities that also build sustainable livelihoods to support their long term food security needs. Communities in Cape Mount, Lofa and Grand Kru counties in Liberia are affected by drought, bush fires and seasonal flooding which, combined with conflict over land tenure and land ownership systems and the resulting conflict, results in a vicious cycle of land degradation, conflict and food insecurity. The project will be carried out in the communities of in the diocesan areas of Cape Mount, Grand Cru and Lofa with rural communities&#x2019; dependant upon agriculture and access to farming land for their livelihoods and that are affected by a combination of drought, bush fires and wind storms and conflict over land tenure.</narrative>
  </description>
